{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b47-fd6f-7658-955e-debf3953770e","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/frontend-design/SKILL.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\n\\n   234\\t- `navigator.share` is allowed inside the share frame (passkeys are not). Feature-detect it, call it only from a click, catch errors and fall back to copying.\\n   235\\t- Share intents (X, Telegram, WhatsApp, `mailto:`, `sms:`): always `encodeURIComponent(link)` and open with `target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"`. A bearer link sent through an intent or a backend reaches that service's servers, so keep its key single-use.\\n   236\\t- When a backend builds links (emails, notifications), the client sends `await getShareBase()` to the server, which validates it against the Studio origins plus its own host before using it.\\n   237\\t- Navigate inside the app with relative links. Never set `window.top.location` or send `window.location` to another site: the frame blocks it and the visitor lands on an \\\"Open app\\\" fallback. Open outside sites with `<a target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">`.\\n   238\\t\\n   239\\t### Address-bar sync (installShareSync)\\n   240\\t\\n   241\\tApps built from the starter already ship `installShareSync()` in `src/lib/share.ts` and call it once from `src/main.tsx`; it mirrors the visitor's in-app path and query into the studio.arc.io address bar. Import it, never overwrite the file, call it once at startup, keep the call whenever you rewrite `src/main.tsx` or `src/lib/share.ts`, and never remove it. Next.js apps call `installShareSync()` from a client component effect in the root layout, guarded by `typeof window !== 'undefined'`; multi-page apps call it on every HTML entry. Only an app that lacks it (older or imported) should add the function below to `src/lib/share.ts`, where it reuses `parentStudioOrigins` from the helper above, and call `installShareSync()` once at startup in `src/main.tsx`. It never sends the `#fragment`, and every path and query it mirrors lands in browser history, so keep secrets out of the path and query.\\n   242\\t\\n   243\\t```ts\\n   244\\tlet syncInstalled = false;\\n   245\\t\\n   246\\texport function installShareSync(): void {\\n   247\\t  if (window.self === window.top || syncInstalled) return;\\n   248\\t  syncInstalled = true;\\n   249\\t  const targets = parentStudioOrigins(window.location.ancestorOrigins, document.referrer);\\n   250\\t  let lastPosted: string | undefined;\\n   251\\t  let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\\n   252\\t  const post = () => {\\n   253\\t    const key = location.pathname + location.search;\\n   254\\t    if (key === lastPosted) return;\\n   255\\t    lastPosted = key;\\n   256\\t    for (const origin of targets) {\\n   257\\t      window.parent.postMessage({ type: 'arc-share:navigated', path: location.pathname, search: location.search }, origin);\\n   258\\t    }\\n   259\\t  };\\n   260\\t  const schedule = () => {\\n   261\\t    timer ??= setTimeout(() => {\\n   262\\t      timer = undefined;\\n   263\\t      post();\\n   264\\t    }, 100);\\n   265\\t  };\\n   266\\t  for (const method of ['pushState', 'replaceState'] as const) {\\n   267\\t    const original = history[method];\\n   268\\t    history[method] = function (this: History, ...args: Parameters<History['pushState']>) {\\n   269\\t      const result = original.apply(this, args);\\n   270\\t      schedule();\\n   271\\t      return result;\\n   272\\t    };\\n   273\\t  }\\n   274\\t  window.addEventListener('popstate', schedule);\\n   275\\t  post();\\n   276\\t}\\n   277\\t```\\n   278\\t\\n   279\\t## NEVER\\n   280\\t\\n   281\\t- Inter, Roboto, Arial, system fonts\\n   282\\t- Purple/blue gradients on white\\n   283\\t- Cookie-cutter layouts\\n   284\\t- Emojis in UI/copy/branding (use icons instead)\\n   285\\t- Animations on layout properties (`width`, `height`, `margin`, `padding`)\\n   286\\t- Simulated balances, addresses, transaction progress, APY, prices, or hashes\\n   287\\t- Default to dark + blue/green without considering if it serves the user\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_014x4sw5VZ7t5jXpiupt38qS\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b47-fd6e-7379-9898-29c72d2863d2","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/context/phase1/spec/ShiftProof-frontend.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\neployments.json` at build time. The shape below is illustrative; do not duplicate addresses in two sources:\\n   187\\t\\n   188\\t```ts\\n   189\\texport const DEPLOYMENTS = {\\n   190\\t  testnet: {\\n   191\\t    chainId: 5042002,\\n   192\\t    name: \\\"Arc Testnet\\\",\\n   193\\t    rpc: \\\"https://rpc.testnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   194\\t    explorer: \\\"https://explorer.testnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   195\\t    usdc: \\\"0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000\\\",\\n   196\\t    contract: \\\"0x...\\\",       // filled after Studio deploy\\n   197\\t    deploymentBlock: 0,      // filled from the receipt\\n   198\\t  },\\n   199\\t  mainnet: {\\n   200\\t    chainId: 5042,\\n   201\\t    name: \\\"Arc Mainnet\\\",\\n   202\\t    rpc: \\\"https://rpc.mainnet.arc.io\\\",\\n   203\\t    explorer: \\\"https://explorer.arc.io\\\",\\n   204\\t    usdc: \\\"0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000\\\",\\n   205\\t    contract: \\\"0x...\\\",       // filled after human deploy\\n   206\\t    deploymentBlock: 0,\\n   207\\t  },\\n   208\\t} as const;\\n   209\\t```\\n   210\\t\\n   211\\t- The app defaults to mainnet for the submission build; a `?network=testnet` query or a build flag selects testnet.\\n   212\\t- `deployments.json` is committed and is the single source of truth for addresses.\\n   213\\t- No runtime admin can change the contract address. A change requires a new build and a new deployment; the repo history shows it.\\n   214\\t\\n   215\\t### 13.10 Hosting options\\n   216\\t\\n   217\\t\\n   218\\t\\n   219\\t### 14.4 Fork and integration tests\\n   220\\t\\n   221\\t- `arc-forge test --network arc` against Arc Testnet runtime `[V: docs deploy-on-arc]`.\\n   222\\t- A fork test with the real testnet USDC address `0x3600…0000`; verify `decimals() == 6`, `transfer`/`transferFrom` behavior, and balances.\\n   223\\t- An integration script deploys to testnet, creates two shifts, clocks, attests, claims, refunds, cancels, and asserts the USDC balance changes.\\n   224\\t- Use small testnet amounts (1–2 USDC/hour) to stay within the Circle faucet’s 20 USDC per 2 hours `[V: S§5.1]`.\\n   225\\t\\n   226\\t### 14.5 Frontend and E2E tests\\n   227\\t\\n   228\\tManual E2E with two Rabby accounts on testnet:\\n   229\\t\\n   230\\t1. Employer creates a 4h × 1 USDC shift; worker is a different address. Approve exact 4 USDC; create.\\n   231\\t2. Worker connects, sees the shift, clocks in/out.\\n   232\\t3. Employer attests 4h; worker claims 4 USDC; balances and receipt match.\\n   233\\t4. Employer creates a 2h × 1 USDC shift; attests 1h; anyone refunds 1 USDC; worker claims 1 USDC.\\n   234\\t5. Employer creates a 1h × 1 USDC shift; cancels before clock-in; full refund.\\n   235\\t6. Wrong wallet: employer tries to claim; worker tries to attest; UI explains before signing.\\n   236\\t7. Wrong network: switch to Ethereum; app disables writes and offers Arc.\\n   237\\t8. Insufficient gas: drain the test wallet; app shows the shortfall.\\n   238\\t9. Refresh/reopen: local history and public receipt still work; no backend.\\n   239\\t10. Mobile viewport: buttons and amounts are readable; wallet connect works in the Rabby browser.\\n   240\\t\\n   241\\tIf Vitest is added, unit-test the amount formatter, status labels, and error decoder. Do not add a heavy E2E framework at the expense of the mainnet proof.\\n   242\\t\\n   243\\t### 14.6 Mainnet rehearsal\\n   244\\t\\n   245\\t- Read `eth_chainId` (5042), `USDC.decimals()` (6), and the deployer/worker balances before any signature `[V: B1, B2, N3]`.\\n   246\\t- Simulate `createShift`, `attest`, `claim`, `refundUnused`, and `cancel` with `eth_call`/`simulateContract` from the actual wallets. A simulation is not a guarantee, but it catches guards/allowance errors.\\n   247\\t- Execute the smallest possible real shift first (e.g., 1 USDC total) to validate the full path before the 20/10 USDC demo shifts. This is a real mainnet transaction and needs per-tx approval.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01WfYydJ7p1zoQ1Z58yELZin\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
