{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-094a-761c-8971-5e98ee05c87f","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/frontend-design/references/arc-modes.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\nrough a runtime `<style>{...}</style>` tag inside a component: browsers only honor `@import` at the very top of a real stylesheet, so the font `@import` in a React-injected `<style>` is silently dropped and the fonts never load; and `:root` variables defined in a runtime `<style>` can be missing on the first paint, so the app renders unstyled.\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t## Arc Light\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\tUse for consumer money apps and games: earn, wallet, bank, checkout, onboarding, deposits, withdrawals, tipping, friendly payment flows, rewards games, raffles, quests, and campaign apps.\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t```css\\n    12\\t:root {\\n    13\\t  --bg: #ffffff;\\n    14\\t  --bg-gradient: linear-gradient(180deg, #f9f9fc 0%, #fffcf7 52%, #fbf7f2 100%);\\n    15\\t  --surface: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);\\n    16\\t  --surface-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.90);\\n    17\\t  --surface-muted: #f5f5f8;\\n    18\\t  --ink: #122d45;\\n    19\\t  --ink-2: #334155;\\n    20\\t  --muted: #6b6580;\\n    21\\t  --subtle: #8a849c;\\n    22\\t  --border: rgba(18, 45, 69, 0.12);\\n    23\\t  --border-strong: rgba(25, 53, 77, 0.50);\\n    24\\t  --accent: #122d45;\\n    25\\t  --accent-hover: #1061a6;\\n    26\\t  --focus: #85b1ed;\\n    27\\t  --success: #1a8047;\\n    28\\t  --danger: #ba2b4c;\\n    29\\t}\\n    30\\t```\\n    31\\t\\n    32\\tPrimary CTA in Arc Light is dark navy (`--accent`) with white text. Secondary actions use translucent white or muted surface.\\n    33\\t\\n    34\\t## Arc Dark\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\tUse for trading, live prices, bridges, infrastructure dashboards, oracle data, and dense charts. Do not use Arc Dark as the default for games; use it only when the user asks for a dark/immersive game or the game is data-dense.\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t```css\\n    39\\t:root {\\n    40\\t  --bg: #0d1b2f;\\n    41\\t  --bg-gradient: linear-gradient(180deg, #0d1b2f 0%, #0d1b2f 58%, #122d45 100%);\\n    42\\t  --surface: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);\\n    43\\t  --surface-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.11);\\n    44\\t  --surface-muted: #1f2f44;\\n    45\\t  --ink: #f9faf3;\\n    46\\t  --ink-2: #e3ecf9;\\n    47\\t  --muted: #cbd5e1;\\n    48\\t  --subtle: #94a3b8;\\n    49\\t  --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);\\n    50\\t  --border-strong: rgba(203, 219, 242, 0.55);\\n    51\\t  --accent: #acc6e9;\\n    52\\t  --accent-hover: #cbdbf2;\\n    53\\t  --success: #8dd89f;\\n    54\\t  --danger: #e86d7a;\\n    55\\t}\\n    56\\t```\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\tPrimary CTA in Arc Dark is light blue (`--accent`) with deep navy text. Do not default to blue/green neon crypto styling.\\n    59\\t\\n    60\\t## Typography\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\tUse Space Grotesk for hero amounts and titles. Use DM Sans for controls, body copy, sheets, tabs, and lists.\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t**Load the fonts** in `index.html` with a `<link>` in `<head>` (preferred), or as an `@import` on the **first line** of `src/index.css`, before the `@tailwind` directives:\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\t```html\\n    67\\t<!-- index.html, inside <head> -->\\n    68\\t<link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\\\" />\\n    69\\t<link rel=\\\"preconnect\\\" href=\\\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\\\" crossorigin />\\n    70\\t<link\\n    71\\t  rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\"\\n    72\\t  href=\\\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap\\\"\\n    73\\t/>\\n    74\\t```\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t**Add the font rules** to `src/index.css`. The scaffold already sets `* { box-sizing }` and `body { margin: 0; min-height: 100dvh }`, so only the font families and helper classes are new:\\n    77\\t\\n    78\\t```css\\n    79\\t/* src/index.css */\\n    80\\tbody { font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; }\\n    81\\t.display { font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif; letter-spacing: -0.03em; }\\n    82\\t.mono { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', Menlo, monospace; }\\n    83\\t```\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_0143tggvPc1SGDMG1ghHhrgg\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-094b-7547-bb6b-04c9655f42e7","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/frontend-design/references/money-components.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\n 47\\t  />\\n    48\\t  <div className=\\\"mt-2 flex items-center justify-between\\\">\\n    49\\t    <span className=\\\"text-xs\\\" style={{ color: 'var(--subtle)' }}>USDC</span>\\n    50\\t    <button\\n    51\\t      disabled={!liveBalance}\\n    52\\t      onClick={() => liveBalance && setAmount(liveBalance)}\\n    53\\t      className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold disabled:opacity-40\\\"\\n    54\\t      style={{ color: 'var(--accent-hover)' }}\\n    55\\t    >\\n    56\\t      {liveBalance ? `Balance: ${formattedBalance} · Max` : 'Balance unavailable'}\\n    57\\t    </button>\\n    58\\t  </div>\\n    59\\t</div>\\n    60\\t```\\n    61\\t\\n    62\\tQuick amount chips are useful for add-money flows. Keep them hidden for precision-heavy swaps unless they help.\\n    63\\t\\n    64\\t## Bottom Sheet\\n    65\\t\\n    66\\tUse sheets for add money, cash out, send, confirm, and settings flows.\\n    67\\t\\n    68\\t```tsx\\n    69\\t<AnimatePresence>\\n    70\\t  {open && (\\n    71\\t    <motion.div className=\\\"fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-end justify-center\\\" initial={{ opacity: 0 }} animate={{ opacity: 1 }} exit={{ opacity: 0 }} onClick={onClose}>\\n    72\\t      <div className=\\\"absolute inset-0 bg-black/25 backdrop-blur-sm\\\" />\\n    73\\t      <motion.section\\n    74\\t        className=\\\"relative w-full max-w-md overflow-hidden rounded-t-3xl\\\"\\n    75\\t        style={{ background: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.88)', backdropFilter: 'blur(40px) saturate(200%)', WebkitBackdropFilter: 'blur(40px) saturate(200%)' }}\\n    76\\t        initial={{ y: '100%' }}\\n    77\\t        animate={{ y: 0 }}\\n    78\\t        exit={{ y: '100%' }}\\n    79\\t        transition={springs.sheet}\\n    80\\t        onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}\\n    81\\t      >\\n    82\\t        {isConsumerMoneyFlow && <div className=\\\"h-1\\\" style={{ background: spectral }} />}\\n    83\\t        <div className=\\\"flex justify-center pt-3 pb-1\\\">\\n    84\\t          <div className=\\\"h-1 w-10 rounded-full bg-black/10\\\" />\\n    85\\t        </div>\\n    86\\t        <div className=\\\"px-5 pb-6 pt-2\\\">{children}</div>\\n    87\\t      </motion.section>\\n    88\\t    </motion.div>\\n    89\\t  )}\\n    90\\t</AnimatePresence>\\n    91\\t```\\n    92\\t\\n    93\\tUse the spectral strip only for consumer money flows, not trading/data screens.\\n    94\\t\\n    95\\t## Transaction CTA\\n    96\\t\\n    97\\tRender transaction states from real domain hooks. Do not time through states.\\n    98\\t\\n    99\\t```tsx\\n   100\\t<button\\n   101\\t  disabled={!ready || isPending || isConfirming}\\n   102\\t  onClick={onAction}\\n   103\\t  className=\\\"w-full rounded-2xl py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:scale-[1.01] active:scale-[0.99] disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-40\\\"\\n   104\\t  style={{ background: 'var(--accent)' }}\\n   105\\t>\\n   106\\t  {!isConnected ? 'Connect Wallet'\\n   107\\t    : wrongChain ? 'Switch to Arc Testnet'\\n   108\\t    : isPending ? <span className=\\\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2\\\"><Loader2 className=\\\"size-4 animate-spin\\\" /> Confirm in wallet...</span>\\n   109\\t    : isConfirming ? <span className=\\\"flex items-center justify-center gap-2\\\"><Loader2 className=\\\"size-4 animate-spin\\\" /> Confirming...</span>\\n   110\\t    : label}\\n   111\\t</button>\\n   112\\t```\\n   113\\t\\n   114\\t## Receipt\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t```tsx\\n   117\\t{isSuccess && txUrl && (\\n   118\\t  <div className=\\\"rounded-2xl p-4\\\" style={glass.inner}>\\n   119\\t    <div className=\\\"text-sm font-semibold\\\" style={{ color: 'var(--success)' }}>Confirmed</div>\\n   120\\t    <a href={txUrl} target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noreferrer\\\" className=\\\"mt-2 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs\\\">\\n   121\\t      View on ArcScan <ExternalLink className=\\\"size-3\\\" />\\n   122\\t    </a>\\n   123\\t  </div>\\n   124\\t)}\\n   125\\t```\\n   126\\t\\n   127\\tShow explorer links only for real transactions.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_019hnN3wJLiy4u5USn5iTppe\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-094c-75dc-882e-11812c15d2c1","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/frontend-design/references/design-review-checklist.md","limit":200},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\t# Design Review Checklist\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tRun this before declaring UI work done.\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\t## Must Fix\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t- UI uses Inter, Roboto, Arial, or raw `system-ui` as the visible brand font.\\n     8\\t- Primary CTA is Tailwind default `bg-blue-600`, `bg-indigo-600`, or purple gradient.\\n     9\\t- Hero uses a generic blue/purple/pink trust gradient.\\n    10\\t- Emojis appear in UI, feature icons, nav, empty states, or branding.\\n    11\\t- Balances, addresses, transaction hashes, APY, odds, or prices are fabricated.\\n    12\\t- Transaction progress moves on a timer instead of real domain state.\\n    13\\t- A \\\"View on explorer\\\" link appears without a real transaction.\\n    14\\t- Buttons lack disabled, loading, pressed, and focus/hover states.\\n    15\\t- Numbers are not `tabular-nums`.\\n    16\\t- Text contrast fails on glass or dark surfaces.\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\t## Should Fix\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t- Accent appears more than twice in the first viewport.\\n    21\\t- Rainbow/spectral detail appears in trading, oracle, bridge, or dense dashboard screens.\\n    22\\t- Every card has identical radius, padding, border, and shadow.\\n    23\\t- First viewport has more than one dominant object.\\n    24\\t- Screen has more than one primary CTA.\\n    25\\t- Copy says \\\"Transaction\\\", \\\"Deposit\\\", \\\"Withdraw\\\", or \\\"Approve token\\\" in a consumer surface where \\\"Send\\\", \\\"Add Money\\\", \\\"Cash Out\\\", or \\\"Allow\\\" would be clearer.\\n    26\\t- Modal/sheet lacks backdrop, drag handle/close affordance, or escape path.\\n    27\\t- Empty/loading/error states are missing for live data.\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t## Good Signs\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t- The app clearly shows connected wallet, network, and live source.\\n    32\\t- Primary action is obvious within 3 seconds.\\n    33\\t- Amount entry and preview make the consequence of action clear.\\n    34\\t- Live values feel alive because they are actually live.\\n    35\\t- Arc Light or Arc Dark tokens are recognizable without making every app identical.\\n    36\\t- Glass and spectral accents are used as finish, not decoration.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01BefzHHni5Ym5bvrQcsHukz\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
