{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"running","toolCallId":"01a17b48-151b-709a-9691-2b01049f481d","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/src/main.tsx","limit":60}}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-1518-7762-a743-d815ef864796","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/onchain-patterns/SKILL.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\n failed. [Reason if available]\\\" | Parse revert reason, suggest common fixes |\\n   448\\t| Network/RPC error | message includes \\\"network\\\" or \\\"timeout\\\" | \\\"Network issue. Check connection and retry.\\\" | Show retry button, preserve user input |\\n   449\\t| Wallet not connected | `useAccount().isDisconnected` | \\\"Connect your wallet to continue.\\\" | Show connect button, disable tx buttons |\\n   450\\t\\n   451\\t### Error Parser Utility\\n   452\\t\\n   453\\t```typescript\\n   454\\texport function parseOnchainError(error: any): string {\\n   455\\t  const message = error?.message?.toLowerCase() || ''\\n   456\\t\\n   457\\t  if (message.includes('user rejected') || error?.code === 4001) {\\n   458\\t    return 'Transaction cancelled.'\\n   459\\t  }\\n   460\\t  if (message.includes('insufficient funds') || message.includes('exceeds balance')) {\\n   461\\t    return 'Insufficient balance. Please add funds and try again.'\\n   462\\t  }\\n   463\\t  if (message.includes('reverted')) {\\n   464\\t    const reasonMatch = message.match(/reason=\\\"([^\\\"]+)\\\"/)\\n   465\\t    return reasonMatch ? `Transaction failed: ${reasonMatch[1]}` : 'Transaction failed. Please try again.'\\n   466\\t  }\\n   467\\t  if (message.includes('network') || message.includes('timeout')) {\\n   468\\t    return 'Network error. Please check your connection and try again.'\\n   469\\t  }\\n   470\\t  return 'Something went wrong. Please try again.'\\n   471\\t}\\n   472\\t```\\n   473\\t\\n   474\\t### Error Handling Best Practices\\n   475\\t\\n   476\\t1. **Never show raw error messages** — parse into user-friendly text\\n   477\\t2. **Preserve user input** — don't clear forms on error\\n   478\\t3. **Provide actionable next steps** — \\\"Switch network\\\", \\\"Add funds\\\", \\\"Try again\\\"\\n   479\\t4. **User rejection is not an error** — just reset state silently\\n   480\\t5. **Use toast for transient errors** (network), inline for action-needed (wrong chain, insufficient funds)\\n   481\\t\\n   482\\t## Strict Rules\\n   483\\t\\n   484\\t- **Always switch to the correct chain before writing to a contract** -- Before any `writeContract` call, check the wallet's current chain via `useAccount().chainId` and call `switchChain()` if it doesn't match the target chain. Executing on the wrong chain will fail or interact with the wrong contract.\\n   485\\t- **No fake addresses** -- Never generate arbitrary wallet addresses. For testing use the connected wallet or require manual input.\\n   486\\t- **No fake payouts in demos** -- Don't add \\\"Claim Payout\\\" that sends FROM the user's wallet (that charges them). For demos show \\\"You won!\\\" without claim; for real payouts use a treasury contract.\\n   487\\t- **Don't render objects in JSX** -- Always extract primitive values before rendering.\\n   488\\t\\n   489\\t## Framework-Specific Configuration\\n   490\\t\\n   491\\t**Next.js:** Add `\\\"use client\\\"` to Web3Provider. Add to `next.config.js`:\\n   492\\t```javascript\\n   493\\tmodule.exports = {\\n   494\\t  webpack: (config) => {\\n   495\\t    config.resolve.fallback = { fs: false, net: false, tls: false }\\n   496\\t    return config\\n   497\\t  },\\n   498\\t}\\n   499\\t```\\n   500\\t\\n   501\\t**Vite:** No special configuration needed.\\n   502\\t\\n   503\\t## Important Notes\\n   504\\t\\n   505\\t### DO NOT\\n   506\\t- Use `as any` to bypass TypeScript errors -- fix the types properly\\n   507\\t- Use 'demo' or fake WalletConnect Project IDs\\n   508\\t- Call wagmi hooks outside of `<ConnectKitProvider>`\\n   509\\t- Mix wagmi v1 hooks with v2+ config\\n   510\\t\\n   511\\t### DO\\n   512\\t- Get a real WalletConnect Project ID from cloud.walletconnect.com\\n   513\\t- Use environment variables for sensitive config\\n   514\\t- Add proper TypeScript types (wagmi has excellent types)\\n   515\\t- Handle loading, error, and success states\\n   516\\t- Test wallet connection in development before production\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01CS2ejyKnnxyBLZxZ1rhZpA\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-151a-74ad-9c00-4f605a1a756b","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/src/config.ts","limit":60},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\t/**\\n     2\\t * wagmi configuration\\n     3\\t * Built with Arc Studio — https://studio.arc.io\\n     4\\t */\\n     5\\t\\n     6\\timport { http, createConfig } from 'wagmi'\\n     7\\timport { mainnet } from 'wagmi/chains'\\n     8\\timport { arcTestnet } from 'viem/chains'\\n     9\\timport { injected } from 'wagmi/connectors'\\n    10\\timport { registerChain } from './tracing'\\n    11\\t\\n    12\\t// Pre-register chain RPC URLs so trace events show correct chain names immediately\\n    13\\tregisterChain(arcTestnet.id, arcTestnet.rpcUrls.default.http[0])\\n    14\\t\\n    15\\texport const config = createConfig({\\n    16\\t  chains: [arcTestnet, mainnet], // mainnet needed for ENS resolution\\n    17\\t  connectors: [injected()],\\n    18\\t  transports: {\\n    19\\t    [arcTestnet.id]: http(),\\n    20\\t    [mainnet.id]: http(), // ENS resolution uses mainnet\\n    21\\t  },\\n    22\\t})\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01NjovJzSGs6be9a3QFPZ6Yi\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-1519-7262-ba4a-d0f0215167db","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/src/App.tsx","limit":50},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\texport default function App() {\\n     2\\t  return (\\n     3\\t    <div className=\\\"min-h-dvh\\\">\\n     4\\t      {/* Build your app here */}\\n     5\\t    </div>\\n     6\\t  )\\n     7\\t}\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01DEUZAk1M9ApZJ4NZ4gnAHe\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b48-151b-709a-9691-2b01049f481d","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/src/main.tsx","limit":60},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\t/*\\n     2\\t *  ███████╗████████╗██╗   ██╗██████╗ ██╗ ██████╗\\n     3\\t *  ██╔════╝╚══██╔══╝██║   ██║██╔══██╗██║██╔═══██╗\\n     4\\t *  ███████╗   ██║   ██║   ██║██║  ██║██║██║   ██║\\n     5\\t *  ╚════██║   ██║   ██║   ██║██║  ██║██║██║   ██║\\n     6\\t *  ███████║   ██║   ╚██████╔╝██████╔╝██║╚██████╔╝\\n     7\\t *  ╚══════╝   ╚═╝    ╚═════╝ ╚═════╝ ╚═╝ ╚═════╝\\n     8\\t *\\n     9\\t *  Built with Arc Studio\\n    10\\t *  https://studio.arc.io\\n    11\\t */\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\timport './tracing'\\n    14\\timport './console-capture'\\n    15\\t\\n    16\\timport { StrictMode } from 'react'\\n    17\\timport { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client'\\n    18\\timport { WagmiProvider } from 'wagmi'\\n    19\\timport { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query'\\n    20\\timport { ConnectKitProvider } from 'connectkit'\\n    21\\timport { Toaster } from 'sonner'\\n    22\\timport { config } from './config'\\n    23\\timport App from './App'\\n    24\\timport './index.css'\\n    25\\t\\n    26\\tconst queryClient = new QueryClient()\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\t// Studio logo SVG\\n    29\\tconst StudioLogo = () => (\\n    30\\t  <svg width=\\\"14\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" viewBox=\\\"0 0 20 22\\\" fill=\\\"none\\\" xmlns=\\\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\\\">\\n    31\\t    <path d=\\\"M0 21.5001C0.167192 16.2366 1.02308 11.3243 2.45378 7.50459C4.26573 2.66517 6.88869 0 9.83904 0C12.7894 0 15.412 2.66517 17.2243 7.50459C18.1669 10.0216 18.8605 13.0121 19.2713 16.2655C19.3081 16.556 19.3393 16.8513 19.3714 17.146C19.3819 17.1642 19.3881 17.1811 19.386 17.1949C19.386 17.1949 19.6275 18.7674 19.6788 21.5001H19.6515C19.2934 21.1937 15.0694 17.7329 8.06739 18.735C8.17304 17.4996 8.31833 16.2974 8.50603 15.1452C8.51562 15.0863 8.52671 15.0294 8.53649 14.9709C11.2828 14.8846 13.6866 15.2171 15.5299 15.6529C15.5231 15.6073 15.5173 15.5603 15.5103 15.5149C15.1314 13.0547 14.5724 10.8024 13.8517 8.87761C12.6732 5.73037 11.1354 3.77496 9.83904 3.77496C8.54269 3.77496 7.00493 5.73037 5.82649 8.87761C5.54123 9.63889 5.28154 10.4508 5.04866 11.3071C4.72126 12.507 4.44621 13.7934 4.22654 15.1451C3.90141 17.1412 3.69827 19.2821 3.62345 21.5001H0Z\\\" fill=\\\"currentColor\\\"/>\\n    32\\t  </svg>\\n    33\\t)\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t// Studio watermark component - links back to Studio\\n    36\\tconst StudioWatermark = () => (\\n    37\\t  <a\\n    38\\t    href=\\\"https://studio.arc.io/\\\"\\n    39\\t    target=\\\"_blank\\\"\\n    40\\t    rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"\\n    41\\t    style={{\\n    42\\t      position: 'fixed',\\n    43\\t      bottom: '16px',\\n    44\\t      right: '16px',\\n    45\\t      display: 'flex',\\n    46\\t      alignItems: 'center',\\n    47\\t      gap: '6px',\\n    48\\t      padding: '8px 14px',\\n    49\\t      fontSize: '12px',\\n    50\\t      fontWeight: 600,\\n    51\\t      fontFamily: 'system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif',\\n    52\\t      color: '#1B3158',\\n    53\\t      textDecoration: 'none',\\n    54\\t      cursor: 'pointer',\\n    55\\t      background: 'rgba(172, 198, 233, 0.85)',\\n    56\\t      backdropFilter: 'blur(12px) saturate(180%)',\\n    57\\t      WebkitBackdropFilter: 'blur(12px) saturate(180%)',\\n    58\\t      borderRadius: '20px',\\n    59\\t      border: '1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4)',\\n    60\\t      zIndex: 9999,\\n\\n[Read 60 lines (lines 1-60 of 82 total). 22 lines remaining from offset 60.]\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_011bVxwZcnTzPwbGXdB5Lqvz\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},