{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b51-64c1-7338-b835-49cbd82fc6d8","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/README.md","limit":10},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"     1\\t# ShiftProof\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tPer-shift USDC escrow and attestation for gig workers. An employer locks USDC into a shift contract; the worker optionally clocks in and out; the employer attests the hours worked; the worker claims their pay; anyone can trigger the residual refund to the employer.\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tBuilt with [Arc Studio](https://studio.arc.io)\\n     6\\t\\n     7\\t## Tech stack\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t- Solidity 0.8.28, EVM Cancun, Foundry\\n    10\\t- OpenZeppelin SafeERC20 + ReentrancyGuard\\n\\n[Read 10 lines (lines 1-10 of 58 total). 48 lines remaining from offset 10.]\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01ErJuGGSPg3YoFHYaLkQKEY\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"tool_start","toolCallId":"01a17b51-6d98-7579-8721-0404781b8cb0","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/README.md","offset":10,"limit":50}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"running","toolCallId":"01a17b51-6d98-7579-8721-0404781b8cb0","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/README.md","offset":10,"limit":50}}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b51-6d98-7579-8721-0404781b8cb0","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/README.md","offset":10,"limit":50},"result":"{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"status\":\"success\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"    11\\t- Target chain: Arc Testnet (5042002) / Arc Mainnet (5042)\\n    12\\t- Token: USDC (6 decimals)\\n    13\\t\\n    14\\t## Deployed contracts\\n    15\\t\\n    16\\t| Network | Address | Explorer |\\n    17\\t|---|---|---|\\n    18\\t| Arc Testnet (5042002) | `0x39845ad25394ec0a6c15ebc5d8968d9c70bb41a6` | [View](https://explorer.testnet.arc.io/address/0x39845ad25394ec0a6c15ebc5d8968d9c70bb41a6) |\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t## Contract files\\n    21\\t\\n    22\\t| File | Purpose |\\n    23\\t|---|---|\\n    24\\t| `contracts/ShiftProof.sol` | Main contract |\\n    25\\t| `contracts/test/ShiftProof.t.sol` | Unit, fuzz, and invariant tests |\\n    26\\t| `contracts/test/MockUSDC.sol` | Test-only ERC-20 mock (never deployed) |\\n    27\\t| `contracts/script/Deploy.s.sol` | Deploy script with chain/USDC pre-flight checks |\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t## Development\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t### Prerequisites\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t- [Bun](https://bun.sh) v1+\\n    34\\t- [Foundry](https://book.getfoundry.sh) (`forge` in PATH)\\n    35\\t\\n    36\\t### Install\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t```bash\\n    39\\tbun install\\n    40\\t```\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t### Build contracts\\n    43\\t\\n    44\\t```bash\\n    45\\tbun run contracts:build\\n    46\\t```\\n    47\\t\\n    48\\t### Test contracts\\n    49\\t\\n    50\\t```bash\\n    51\\tbun run contracts:test\\n    52\\t```\\n    53\\t\\n    54\\tRuns 76 tests: unit matrix (U01-U40), transition matrix (T01-T16), fuzz (rate / duration / attested seconds / random actors), and five Foundry invariants (solvency, totalEscrow sum, owed <= escrow, no double-claim, terminal-state zeroing).\\n    55\\t\\n    56\\t### Environment variables\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\tNone required for building and testing locally. Deploy requires a funded wallet and an RPC endpoint for Arc Mainnet or Testnet; supply them via Foundry's `--rpc-url` and `--private-key` flags (or environment variables) at deploy time.\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01FECGW7xMuPW3SiYox1epLk\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
